++---
++description: "Local repository-plugin loader: mounts the Loader entries a checkout declares in its .dsh-plugin/package.json (dsh.entry)."
++kind: "package-reference"
++---
++
++# @deepseek-ai/dsh-repository-plugin
++
++## Summary
++
++`dsh-repository-plugin` mounts a local checkout's repository plugin: for every configured root it reads `.dsh-plugin/package.json`, resolves the `dsh.entry` module the manifest declares against that directory, and creates one ordinary Loader entry per repository plugin. The mounted plugin therefore appears in the boot graph exactly as a config row would, is addressable in the Loader store, and fails loud through the same activation audit. This restores the on-disk authoring format of the removed repository-Plugin path for local checkouts; package acquisition stays with profile bundles, and the removed remote source list, generated wrapper, preparation executable, and repository cache are deliberately not restored.
++
++## Table of Contents
++
++- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
++- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)
++- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
++
++-----
++
++<a id="use-this-package"></a>
++## Use this package
++
++Compose this plugin from a bundle patch row; the shipped base layer composes it with `roots: ['.']`, so a repository plugin loads when dsh boots from its checkout:
++
++```yaml
++- id: repository-plugin
++  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-repository-plugin'
++  config:
++    roots: ['.']
++```
++
++`roots` are directories, resolved against the boot working directory when relative. `manifest` names the manifest inside each root and defaults to `.dsh-plugin/package.json`. A root without that manifest is not a repository plugin and is skipped.
++
++The mounted repository is trusted code: its entry executes in the host process with the same authority as an installed plugin. Point `roots` only at checkouts whose source you trust, and keep the default `['.']` only in compositions launched from a checkout.
++
++### Observable failures
++
++A root whose manifest exists but cannot be read, is not JSON, or declares no non-empty string `dsh.entry` fails the row at boot; a present manifest that cannot mount is never silently skipped. An entry module that fails to import, or whose plugin waits on a missing service, is reported by the boot activation audit under its entry name. Unloading the row removes the entries it created and joins their teardown.
++
++-----
++
++<a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
++## Understand the implementation
++
++`apply` resolves the configured roots, reads each manifest once, and collects the declared entries before mounting anything, so a malformed manifest fails before the Loader tree changes. Mounting runs inside one `ctx.effect` that owns the created entry ids in creation order: the disposer removes them in reverse, and a failure part-way removes what it created before rethrowing. Entry names are the `file:` URLs of the entry modules, so the Loader resolves each module from the manifest directory rather than from the profile directory.
++
++-----
++
++<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
++## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
++
++- **Local checkouts only** — the removed remote source list (git/npm specifications), its immutable cache, and the preparation executable are not restored; install distributable plugins as profile bundles with `dsh plugin add`.
++- **No per-plugin config** — a manifest declares one entry path and no plugin config, matching the removed wrapper's limitation; a repository needing config should ship a bundle patch.
++- **Bilingual README pending** — `README.zh.md` and the generated catalogs have not been produced for this package.
