+# Harness patches
+
+This directory carries the dsh-side patches the plugin still needs after the
+`dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` review. A patch stays here while a documented capability needs a
+general-purpose harness change that official extension points do not provide; it is not dropped
+because the plugin can degrade without it.
+
+## 0001-restore-repository-plugin-loading.patch
+
+Applies to the `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` source checkout. It restores the local repository-plugin
+loading path — a checkout whose `.dsh-plugin/package.json` declares `dsh.entry` mounts that entry
+as an ordinary Loader row — which dsh removed in 0.1.1-rc.1. Remote source fetching stays with
+profile bundles.
+
+```sh
+cd <dsh source checkout>
+git apply /path/to/patches/0001-restore-repository-plugin-loading.patch
+```
+
+The patch:
+
+- adds `@deepseek-ai/dsh-repository-plugin` under `packages/boot/repository-plugin` (loader
+  plugin, invariant companion, package manifest, tsconfig, README, real-composition spec);
+- composes the base bundle row `repository-plugin` with `roots: ['.']`
+  (`packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml`) and declares the package as a dependency of
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-base`, so the bare row name resolves in an installed profile;
+- registers the workspace aliases/aggregates the monorepo resolves that name through
+  (`tsconfig.base.json`, `tsconfig.host.json`) and the new importer in `pnpm-lock.yaml`;
+- pins the row and its dependency in `packages/bundle/base/tests/base.spec.ts`.
+
+The mounted entry name is the entry module's `file:` URL (`pathToFileURL`), the same
+absolute-path convention the Loader itself uses elsewhere; a raw platform path is not a valid
+module specifier on Windows.
+
+Request, evidence, and verification record:
+`.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/restore-repository-plugin-loading/report.md`.
